+---
+type: Procedure
+title: Site delivery
+description: Interpret a deploy hook result and recover a missing site build.
+---
+
+# Site delivery
+
+## Hook delivery
+
+After [publication](../publishing/publication.md), Inkwell posts to the site's
+deploy hook up to three times. Failed network calls and non-success responses
+are retried with a linear delay: 250 ms before the second attempt and 500 ms
+before the third. This short window gives a cold host time to wake up. It cannot
+recover a deleted or misconfigured hook.
+
+On exhaustion the API has no error tracker, so the hook client logs the failure
+at error level and returns `ok: false` instead of throwing. The publish route
+reports `deployTriggered: false` to the editor.
+
+A successful hook response acknowledges the request. The [Acme release receipt](../receipts/hook-17.txt)
+records HTTP 202 for revision 42. Neither that receipt nor the hook implementation
+establishes a maximum time until the customer's site is live. Check the hosting
+agreement before giving a customer a deadline.
+
+## Recover a missed build
+
+Check the site's hosting dashboard for this publication. If its build is
+queued or running, stop and follow that build. Otherwise trigger one rebuild
+from the host dashboard. Leave the published content alone.
