+---
+type: Specification
+title: Publication
+description: What a publish commits and which content a failed hook leaves in place.
+---
+
+# Publication
+
+## Publication transaction
+
+A publish snapshots the saved title and body and marks the post published in one
+transaction. Both writes commit together. A draft save alone adds no revision.
+
+## If the hook fails
+
+Only after commit does Inkwell call the site's hook. The host operates independently:
+if it cannot accept a request, the author still has the published post and revision.
+The publish response reports the outcome in `deployTriggered` and the editor tells
+the author when the deploy failed. For recovery, follow
+[the hosting procedure](../delivery/rebuild.md#recover-a-missed-build).
+
+## Reverting published content
+
+There is no unpublish or automatic undo. To revert the content, edit it back to the
+previous text, save it, then publish again. That produces another revision.
